# Performance & Raspberry Pi Rules

These rules apply to **every change**. The app runs 24/7 on Raspberry Pi 4 hardware with
limited CPU, GPU, and RAM. Every render, allocation, and animation matters.

## Memory Management

### ALWAYS clean up side effects

Every `setInterval`, `setTimeout`, event listener, and subscription MUST be cleaned up
in the `useEffect` return function:

```typescript
// CORRECT: Cleanup on unmount
useEffect(() => {
  const interval = setInterval(tick, 1000);
  const handler = () => dispatch(setOffline(true));
  window.addEventListener('offline', handler);

  return () => {
    clearInterval(interval);
    window.removeEventListener('offline', handler);
  };
}, []);

// WRONG: Memory leak — interval never cleared
useEffect(() => {
  setInterval(tick, 1000);
}, []);
```

### Use refs for non-UI data

If a value is needed for logic but does not trigger a re-render, use `useRef`:

```typescript
// CORRECT: Ref for tracking without re-render
const lastFetchRef = useRef<number>(0);

// WRONG: State for non-UI tracking (causes unnecessary re-render)
const [lastFetch, setLastFetch] = useState(0);
```

### Avoid large objects in state

Do NOT store raw API responses in React state if they contain nested data you never render.
Extract only the fields you need, or store the full response in `storageService` and keep
a lightweight version in Redux.

## Rendering Optimisation

### React.memo for expensive components

Wrap components that receive stable props but have expensive render logic:

```typescript
const PrayerTimesPanel = React.memo(({ prayerTimes, nextPrayer }) => {
  // Expensive grid rendering
}, (prev, next) => {
  return prev.nextPrayer === next.nextPrayer
    && prev.prayerTimes === next.prayerTimes;
});
```

### useMemo for expensive calculations

```typescript
// CORRECT: Memoised
const sortedEvents = useMemo(
  () => events.filter(e => !e.expired).sort((a, b) => a.date - b.date),
  [events]
);

// WRONG: Recalculates every render
const sortedEvents = events.filter(e => !e.expired).sort((a, b) => a.date - b.date);
```

### useCallback for handler references

```typescript
// CORRECT: Stable reference
const handleTick = useCallback(() => {
  dispatch(updateCountdown());
}, [dispatch]);

// WRONG: New function every render (breaks React.memo on children)
const handleTick = () => dispatch(updateCountdown());
```

## CSS Performance Rules

### Use `.gpu-accelerated` for animated elements

The `.gpu-accelerated` class in `src/index.css` applies:
- `transform: translateZ(0)` — promotes to GPU layer
- `will-change: transform` — hints browser to optimise
- `backface-visibility: hidden` — prevents rendering artefacts

Apply it to any element with transitions or animations.

### No backdrop-filter

`backdrop-filter: blur()` is extremely expensive on RPi GPU. Cards use
solid or semi-transparent `rgba()` backgrounds instead.

```css
/* WRONG: Crashes on RPi */
.card { backdrop-filter: blur(10px); }

/* CORRECT: Performant alternative */
.card { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); }
```

### Prefer CSS transitions over JS animations

```tsx
// CORRECT: CSS transition
<div className="transition-opacity duration-normal" style={{ opacity: visible ? 1 : 0 }}>

// WRONG: JS animation loop
useEffect(() => {
  let opacity = 0;
  const frame = () => { opacity += 0.02; el.style.opacity = opacity; requestAnimationFrame(frame); };
  frame();
}, []);
```

### Minimal box-shadow

Heavy `box-shadow` values cause GPU compositing overhead. Use sparingly and
prefer border-based visual separation.

### No external font loading

Fonts (Poppins, Amiri) are self-hosted in `src/assets/fonts/`. Do NOT add `@import`
from Google Fonts or any other CDN — this breaks offline mode and adds latency.

## Build Optimisations

### Terser minification

Production builds use Terser to:
- Drop all `console.*` calls
- Drop `debugger` statements
- Minify and tree-shake

This means `console.log()` will silently disappear in production. Use the logger utility
instead (it has its own persistence).

### Code splitting

`vite.config.ts` defines manual chunks:

| Chunk | Contents |
|---|---|
| `vendor` | react, react-dom, react-router-dom |
| `redux` | @reduxjs/toolkit, react-redux, redux-persist |
| `io` | socket.io-client, axios |

Do NOT remove these splits. They ensure the main bundle stays small and cacheable.

### No source maps in production

`sourcemap: false` in `vite.config.ts`. Do NOT enable source maps for production
builds — they bloat the bundle and are not useful on a kiosk display.

## PWA / Service Worker

Configured via `vite-plugin-pwa` in `vite.config.ts`:

| URL Pattern | Strategy | Cache TTL |
|---|---|---|
| API calls (`/api/`) | NetworkFirst (10s timeout) | 24 hours, 50 entries max |
| Images (`.png`, `.jpg`, `.svg`, etc.) | CacheFirst | 30 days, 100 entries max |
| Fonts (`.woff`, `.woff2`, etc.) | CacheFirst | 1 year, 20 entries max |
| Static assets (`.js`, `.css`, `.html`) | Precached via globPatterns | Immutable (hashed filenames) |

Registration type: `autoUpdate` — the service worker updates silently without prompting.

## Logging

### ALWAYS use the logger utility

```typescript
import logger from '@/utils/logger';

// CORRECT
logger.info('[PrayerTimes] Next prayer calculated', { name, time });
logger.error('[Sync] Failed to refresh content', { error: err.message });
logger.debug('[Carousel] Slide transition', { from: idx, to: nextIdx });
logger.warn('[Network] Connection lost, using cached data');

// WRONG — stripped in production, no structured context
console.log('next prayer:', name);
```

### Logger levels

| Level | Use for | Production |
|---|---|---|
| `error` | Critical failures that need attention | Kept |
| `warn` | Potential problems, degraded states | Kept |
| `info` | Important state changes, lifecycle events | Kept |
| `debug` | Verbose debugging detail | Dev only |

### Remove debug artefacts before committing

Search for and remove:
- `// #region agent log` blocks
- Stray `console.log()` / `console.warn()` / `console.error()` calls
- `debugger` statements
- Hardcoded test data

## Kiosk Mode Constraints

The display runs in Chromium kiosk mode with these constraints:

- `cursor: none !important` on all elements (set in `src/index.css`)
- No scrollbars, no text selection
- Screen sleep disabled via `xset` (in `deploy/kiosk.sh`)
- Mouse cursor hidden after 0.5s via `unclutter`
- No address bar, no Chrome UI, no error dialogs
- Context menu and keyboard shortcuts prevented by `uiSlice` flags

**Every UI element must be visible and legible without any user interaction.**

## Checklist for Every Change

Before submitting any code change, verify:

- [ ] All `setInterval`/`setTimeout`/event listeners cleaned up in `useEffect` return
- [ ] No `console.log()` — use `logger` utility
- [ ] No `backdrop-filter` or heavy `box-shadow`
- [ ] Expensive components wrapped in `React.memo`
- [ ] Expensive calculations wrapped in `useMemo`
- [ ] Handlers wrapped in `useCallback` where passed as props
- [ ] No external CDN dependencies (fonts, scripts, stylesheets)
- [ ] No `any` types unless absolutely unavoidable
- [ ] TypeScript compiles: `npm run build`
- [ ] **Linter passes: run `npm run lint` and fix any reported errors before claiming a change is complete.** Do not say a change is good or done until lint passes (including for files under `rpi-image/`, `deploy/`, and any other paths included in the lint config).
